        "geology": "mica schist, granite, and quartzite bedrock",
        "hydrology": "Specific outlet: Catchment of Certovo Lake: 25-64 (42 on average) l/km2/s in 1998-2011. Catchment of Plesne Lake: 23-57 (35 on average) l/km2/s in 1998-2011.",
        "soils": "Catchment of Certovo Lake is covered with ~0.5 m deep spodo-dystric cambisol (58%), podsol (21%), and shallow (~0.2 m) leptosol (17%); wetlands and bare rocks represent ~3% and 1%, respectively. Catchment of Plesne Lake is covered with ~0.2 m deep leptosol (38%) and ~0.45 m deep podsol (29%) or spodo-dystric cambisol (27%); the rest is bare rocks (5%) and wetlands (~1%).",
        "vegetation": "The catchments weighted means of above-ground biomass of the understory vegetation (mostly Vaccinium myrtillus and Calamagrostis villosa) were 723 and 288 g m?2 in the PL and CT catchments, respectively, in 2004. Forest is dominated by mature Norvay spruce Picea abies), which was seriously damaged by a bark beetle (Ips typographus) outbreak during 2004-2006."
